    "roles": ["session", "band_member", "touring", "producer"],
    "summary": "The drum half of Sly and Robbie, with Robbie Shakespeare from 1972: the Aggrovators, the Upsetters, Channel One's Revolutionaries, Peter Tosh's band, then their own Taxi label, Black Uhuru, Grace Jones, Gainsbourg, Dylan and the Rolling Stones. With the Revolutionaries in 1976 he brought in rockers, the bass drum on every beat where the one drop left the 1 out, and Right Time's double tap on the rim; the hats galloping in sixteenths and eighths; syndrums and later drum machines and electronic drums in the dancehall era. Eno, 1979: 'a 90 percent chance the drummer is Sly Dunbar'. Two Grammys; he died in Kingston in January 2026."
  },
